{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Violence shall no more be heard in your land, devastation nor destruction.</b> The meaning is doubled:" "<b>And you shall call.</b> Some say it is like וקראתם אתם הרעה (Deuteronomy 31:29), and some say it is from the root of calling, for salvation shall call out to your walls. The correct view is that the word וקראת is addressed to Zion, for you shall call your walls 'Salvation,' as evidenced by 'and your gates Praise.' And behold, וקראת draws after it its object, as is the rule."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:31.344687456Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}